<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24352" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημᾰγωγ-ός</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>popular leader,</i> as Cleon or
			Pericles, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				8.126
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἀγαθοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					27.10
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ δίκαιος δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hyp.
					<u>Dem.Fr.</u>
					5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> more freq. in
			bad sense, <i>leader of the mob, demagogue,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				2.3.27
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀχλοκόπος καὶ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					3.80.3
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι δημαγωγοῦ,</span> opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔργα τυράννου,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				And.
				4.27
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔστι γὰρ ὁ δ. τοῦ δήμου κόλαξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1313b40
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1292a20
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
